The adapter delegates hashing and signing to the existing validated AWS-LC key
and EVP signing implementation. It does not copy a cryptographic primitive.
See UPSTREAM.md for exact source pins, opt-in scope and qualification limits.

The same optional feature supplies the existing validated key's modulus bit
count to the native TLS 1.3 RSA-PSS signing-failure alert classifier, following
Go 1.26.9 crypto/tls/handshake_server_tls13.go. Existing AWS EVP wrappers and
RSA signing operations remain unchanged. Go BSD terms remain in LICENSE-GO.
